<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
   CardDemo — Greenfield Java 25 LTS + Spring Boot 3.x Migration
   Root Maven Build Manifest (single source of truth for the dependency closure)
  ============================================================================

   PROVENANCE & TRACEABILITY
   This is a brand-new, greenfield build manifest. It has NO source equivalent in
   the legacy estate. The migrated Java application is a standalone project; the
   original AWS CardDemo COBOL/CICS/VSAM/JCL/BMS sources are NOT copied into this
   repository. Traceability to the frozen legacy baseline is by original COBOL
   repository commit SHA: 27d6c6f (see AAP §0.7.2 — Preservation Requirements).

   The legacy build/install cadence — the DFHCSDUP resource-install job
   (app/jcl/CBADMCDJ.jcl) plus the BUILDBAT/BUILDBMS/BUILDONL procedures under
   samples/jcl — is wholly REPLACED by this Maven build and the Spring Boot
   plugin. CICS CSD GROUP(CARDDEMO) resource registration (mapsets, programs,
   TRANSIDs) has no Maven analogue: it is realized at runtime by Spring component
   scanning and the @RequestMapping route table.

   MINIMAL CHANGE CLAUSE (AAP §0.7.1)
   The dependency surface is intentionally limited to EXACTLY the inventory the
   authoritative blueprint enumerates (docs/technical-specifications.md L728–L766).
   No convenience libraries (e.g. Lombok) or code-generation tooling are added.
   Each technology-substitution point (VSAM→JPA, CICS TDQ→SQS, GDG→S3,
   3270/BMS→REST, plaintext USRSEC→BCrypt, CEEDAYS→java.time) is documented at the
   point of declaration below.

   BLUEPRINT INCONSISTENCIES RESOLVED HERE
   1. Base package / groupId = com.cardemo (authoritative structure diagram,
      tech-spec L334 & L476). The import-table variant "com.carddemo" is rejected
      so a single base package is applied uniformly across the target.
   2. JaCoCo plugin version = 0.8.14 (NOT 0.8.12). Java 25 emits class-file major
      version 69; JaCoCo gained OFFICIAL Java 25 support in 0.8.14 (0.8.13 was
      experimental only). Versions < 0.8.13 fail instrumentation with
      "Unsupported class file major version 69". The blueprint dependency table
      (L766) cited 0.8.12 as a baseline; per its own fallback rule we pin 0.8.14
      so `mvn clean verify` can run JaCoCo under Java 25 without error.

   SECURITY / CVE REMEDIATION (AAP §0.7.8 — zero critical/high CVE gate)
   The dependency closure is pinned to versions whose resolved transitive graph
   passes `dependency-check-maven` with the CVSS>=7 gate (failBuildOnCVSS=7). The
   only changes are version bumps — no dependency is added or removed, preserving
   the Minimal Change Clause (§0.7.1):
   1. Spring Boot parent 3.5.11 -> 3.5.15. The 3.5.15 managed BOM advances the
      transitive closure to non-vulnerable releases: tomcat-embed 10.1.52->10.1.55
      (CVE-2026-41293/-34483/-29129/-41284), spring-boot 3.5.11->3.5.15
      (CVE-2026-40971), and spring-framework 6.2.16->6.2.19 / angus-mail->2.0.5
      (CVE-2026-41838/-41851/-41842, CVE-2025-7962).
   2. Netty pinned to 4.1.135.Final via an io.netty:netty-bom import declared
      FIRST in <dependencyManagement> (below). The Spring Cloud AWS 3.3.0 closure
      transitively imports the AWS SDK BOM, which pins netty to 4.1.131.Final
      (CVE-2026-42585/-33870); a first-declared netty-bom import wins over a later
      imported BOM for the same GA, lifting netty to the patched 4.1.135.Final
      (the same version the Spring Boot 3.5.15 BOM expects).
   3. opentelemetry-semconv pinned to the current 1.41.1 (io.opentelemetry.semconv
      group) via an explicit <dependencyManagement> entry. This artifact has its
      own release train (NOT the Spring Boot `opentelemetry.version`) and arrived
      transitively at 1.32.0; 1.41.1 is the current release of this generated-
      constants jar.

   JUSTIFIED CVE SUPPRESSIONS (owasp-suppressions.xml, wired into the plugin below)
   After the version bumps above, the only residual CVSS>=7 matches are five
   CPE/scope false positives where dependency-check matched a shared CPE to the
   wrong artifact (or to a module that is absent from this closure). Each is
   suppressed for the SPECIFIC CVE only, with a documented rationale in
   owasp-suppressions.xml (verified against the dependency tree):
     - org.eclipse.angus:angus-activation  CVE-2025-7962 — the flaw is Jakarta/
       Angus *Mail* SMTP injection (CPE eclipse:angus_mail / eclipse:jakarta_mail);
       this is the Jakarta *Activation* impl. No mail artifact is on the classpath.
     - org.apache.logging.log4j:log4j-api  CVE-2026-34478/-34479/-34480/-34481 —
       all four are Log4j *Core* layout classes (Rfc5424/Log4j1Xml/Xml/JsonTemplate);
       only the log4j-*api* facade is present (via log4j-to-slf4j). log4j-core is
       absent, so the vulnerable classes can never be loaded.
     - io.micrometer:micrometer-registry-prometheus  CVE-2026-42154 — the flaw is
       the Prometheus *Go server* /api/v1/read endpoint (CPE prometheus:prometheus,
       v3.x); this is the Micrometer Java client that merely exposes metrics.
     - io.netty:* (netty-transport, netty-transport-classes-epoll, ...)
       CVE-2026-42582 — the flaw is in netty-codec-*http3* (4.2.x line), a module
       ABSENT from this closure (only netty-codec-http2 is present). The netty:netty
       CPE range lacks a lower bound, over-matching every 4.1.x netty module. The
       fix (4.2.13) requires Netty 4.2.x, which cannot share a classpath with 4.1.x
       and needs Spring Boot 4.x — outside the Minimal Change Clause (§0.7.1).
     - io.opentelemetry.semconv:opentelemetry-semconv  CVE-2026-39883 — the flaw is
       in OpenTelemetry-*Go* (Darwin `ioreg`); the CPE targets the `go` platform.
       This is a Java constants jar with no command/exec logic.
    For final-evidence completeness, owasp-suppressions.xml ALSO documents five
    informational MEDIUM (CVSS < 7.0, below this gate) CPE/version false positives
    so the persisted report is pristine (zero reported): log4j-api SocketAppender
    CVE-2025-68161/-34477 (Log4j *Core*, absent), hibernate-validator CVE-2025-15104
    (Nu Html Checker validator.nu, a different product), kotlin-stdlib(+jdk7)
    CVE-2020-29582 (fixed in Kotlin 1.4.21; resolved at 1.9.25), and
    opentelemetry-semconv CVE-2026-39882 (OpenTelemetry-Go OTLP exporter). The
    passing HTML+JSON report is persisted under docs/evidence/owasp/.
  ============================================================================
-->
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">

    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <!--
      Spring Boot managed parent. Supplies the dependency BOM (consistent,
      curated versions for all Spring Boot starters and the wider ecosystem) and
      sensible plugin defaults. Empty <relativePath/> forces resolution from the
      repository rather than a parent directory on disk.
    -->
    <parent>
        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>
        <version>3.5.15</version>
        <relativePath/>
    </parent>

    <!-- Project coordinates. Base package == groupId == com.cardemo (see header). -->
    <groupId>com.cardemo</groupId>
    <artifactId>carddemo-java</artifactId>
    <version>1.0.0</version>
    <packaging>jar</packaging>

    <name>CardDemo Java</name>
    <description>
        Greenfield Java 25 LTS + Spring Boot 3.x migration of the AWS CardDemo
        COBOL/CICS/VSAM/JCL/BMS mainframe application. Exposes the legacy online
        transactions as stateless REST endpoints and the legacy JCL batch suite as
        Spring Batch jobs, over a PostgreSQL data layer (Spring Data JPA) with AWS
        S3/SQS/SNS integration. Behavioral parity with the COBOL baseline is
        preserved; BigDecimal is used for every COMP-3/COMP/PIC decimal field.
    </description>

    <properties>
        <!-- Java 25 LTS / OpenJDK 25.0.2 (AAP §0.5.1). Both the Spring Boot
             convention property (java.version) and the explicit compiler release
             are set so the compiler targets class-file major version 69. -->
        <java.version>25</java.version>
        <maven.compiler.release>25</maven.compiler.release>

        <!-- Deterministic, platform-independent encoding for sources & reports. -->
        <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
        <project.reporting.outputEncoding>UTF-8</project.reporting.outputEncoding>

        <!-- Versions for dependencies NOT governed by the Spring Boot 3.5.15 BOM. -->
        <!-- Spring Cloud AWS is an independent release train (io.awspring.cloud);
             its BOM MUST be imported below or the starters have no version. -->
        <spring-cloud-aws.version>3.3.0</spring-cloud-aws.version>
        <!-- Testcontainers ships its own BOM (imported below). -->
        <testcontainers.version>2.0.3</testcontainers.version>
        <!-- Structured JSON logging encoder — not BOM-managed; pinned explicitly. -->
        <logstash-logback-encoder.version>8.0</logstash-logback-encoder.version>

        <!-- SECURITY OVERRIDES (AAP §0.7.8 zero critical/high CVE gate; see header). -->
        <!-- Netty: the Spring Cloud AWS 3.3.0 closure transitively pins netty to
             4.1.131.Final (CVE-2026-42585/-33870). A netty-bom import declared FIRST
             in <dependencyManagement> below lifts it to the patched 4.1.135.Final
             (the version the Spring Boot 3.5.15 BOM also expects). -->
        <netty.version>4.1.135.Final</netty.version>
        <!-- OpenTelemetry SemConv: own release train (io.opentelemetry.semconv),
             NOT the Spring Boot opentelemetry.version. Arrived transitively at
             1.32.0; pinned to the current 1.41.1 below. Its residual CVE-2026-39883
             match is an OpenTelemetry-Go platform false positive (CPE targets `go`);
             justified suppression lives in owasp-suppressions.xml. -->
        <opentelemetry-semconv.version>1.41.1</opentelemetry-semconv.version>

        <!-- Build-plugin versions. -->
        <!-- JaCoCo 0.8.14 = official Java 25 (class-file major 69) support. -->
        <jacoco.version>0.8.14</jacoco.version>
        <!-- OWASP dependency-check for the "zero critical/high CVE" gate (§0.7.8). -->
        <owasp-dependency-check.version>12.1.0</owasp-dependency-check.version>
        <!-- Surefire (unit) and Failsafe (integration) share one pinned version. -->
        <maven-surefire-failsafe.version>3.5.2</maven-surefire-failsafe.version>

        <!-- Integration/E2E tests require Docker (Testcontainers) so they are
             skipped by default and enabled via the `integration` profile, which
             realizes the `mvn verify -Pintegration` workflow (tech-spec L979). -->
        <skipITs>true</skipITs>
    </properties>

    <!--
      dependencyManagement: import BOMs for the two dependency families the Spring
      Boot parent does NOT manage. Importing these (type=pom, scope=import) lets
      the corresponding <dependencies> entries below omit explicit <version> tags.
    -->
    <dependencyManagement>
        <dependencies>
            <!-- SECURITY OVERRIDE — netty-bom MUST be the FIRST import (AAP §0.7.8).
                 Maven resolves a managed GA from the first-declared import; declaring
                 io.netty:netty-bom ahead of spring-cloud-aws-dependencies (which
                 transitively imports the AWS SDK BOM pinning netty 4.1.131.Final,
                 CVE-2026-42585/-33870) lifts every netty-* module to the patched
                 4.1.135.Final. Behavior-neutral version bump only. (The residual
                 CVE-2026-42582 is a netty-codec-http3 4.2.x-line flaw; that module
                 is absent here — justified suppression in owasp-suppressions.xml.) -->
            <dependency>
                <groupId>io.netty</groupId>
                <artifactId>netty-bom</artifactId>
                <version>${netty.version}</version>
                <type>pom</type>
                <scope>import</scope>
            </dependency>
            <!-- VERSION HYGIENE — OpenTelemetry SemConv (io.opentelemetry.semconv).
                 Its own release train (NOT the Spring Boot opentelemetry.version);
                 arrived transitively at 1.32.0. Pinned to the current 1.41.1. Its
                 residual CVE-2026-39883 is an OpenTelemetry-Go false positive
                 (justified suppression in owasp-suppressions.xml). -->
            <dependency>
                <groupId>io.opentelemetry.semconv</groupId>
                <artifactId>opentelemetry-semconv</artifactId>
                <version>${opentelemetry-semconv.version}</version>
            </dependency>
            <!-- Spring Cloud AWS (S3/SQS/SNS) — independent of the Spring Boot BOM. -->
            <dependency>
                <groupId>io.awspring.cloud</groupId>
                <artifactId>spring-cloud-aws-dependencies</artifactId>
                <version>${spring-cloud-aws.version}</version>
                <type>pom</type>
                <scope>import</scope>
            </dependency>
            <!-- Testcontainers — manages postgresql/localstack/junit-jupiter modules. -->
            <dependency>
                <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
                <artifactId>testcontainers-bom</artifactId>
                <version>${testcontainers.version}</version>
                <type>pom</type>
                <scope>import</scope>
            </dependency>
        </dependencies>
    </dependencyManagement>

    <dependencies>
        <!-- ====================================================================
             RUNTIME DEPENDENCIES (17) — docs/technical-specifications.md L728–L744
             Versions marked "(BOM)" are managed by the Spring Boot 3.5.15 parent.
             ==================================================================== -->

        <!-- REST API framework + embedded Tomcat. Replaces the BMS 3270 SEND/RECEIVE
             MAP presentation tier with stateless REST endpoints (3270→REST). -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!-- JPA/Hibernate ORM. Replaces VSAM KSDS keyed access with relational
             access over PostgreSQL (VSAM→JPA repositories). -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-data-jpa</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Spring Batch. Replaces the JCL/JES batch suite (POSTTRAN, INTCALC,
             COMBTRAN, CREASTMT, TRANREPT) with Job/Step/Flow orchestration. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-batch</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Spring Security. Provides BCrypt password hashing, upgrading the legacy
             plaintext USRSEC store (constraint C-003) — the single permitted
             behavioral change — while preserving the sign-on flow. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-security</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Jakarta Bean Validation. Replaces COBOL field edits and the CSSETATY
             attribute copybook with declarative @Valid field constraints. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-validation</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Actuator. Health/readiness probes and the metrics endpoint required by
             the observability requirement (tech-spec §0.8.6). -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-actuator</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!-- AWS S3 client. Replaces sequential PS staging datasets and GDG
             generations with versioned S3 object keys (GDG→S3). Version via the
             imported spring-cloud-aws BOM. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>io.awspring.cloud</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-cloud-aws-starter-s3</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!-- AWS SQS client. Replaces the CICS Transient Data Queue WRITEQ bridge
             (CORPT00C → TDQ 'JOBS' → JES) with an SQS-triggered batch job. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>io.awspring.cloud</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-cloud-aws-starter-sqs</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!-- AWS SNS client. Notification/alert publishing. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>io.awspring.cloud</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-cloud-aws-starter-sns</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!-- PostgreSQL 16+ JDBC driver. Needed only at runtime. Version via parent
             BOM (~42.7.x). -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.postgresql</groupId>
            <artifactId>postgresql</artifactId>
            <scope>runtime</scope>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Flyway schema migration. Replaces IDCAMS DEFINE CLUSTER provisioning;
             V1/V2/V3 scripts create tables, indexes, and seed the ASCII fixtures. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.flywaydb</groupId>
            <artifactId>flyway-core</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.flywaydb</groupId>
            <artifactId>flyway-database-postgresql</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Distributed tracing: Micrometer → OpenTelemetry bridge + OTLP exporter. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>io.micrometer</groupId>
            <artifactId>micrometer-tracing-bridge-otel</artifactId>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>io.opentelemetry</groupId>
            <artifactId>opentelemetry-exporter-otlp</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Prometheus metrics registry (scrape endpoint via Actuator). -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>io.micrometer</groupId>
            <artifactId>micrometer-registry-prometheus</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Structured JSON logging with correlation IDs. NOT BOM-managed — the
             version is pinned via the property above. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>net.logstash.logback</groupId>
            <artifactId>logstash-logback-encoder</artifactId>
            <version>${logstash-logback-encoder.version}</version>
        </dependency>

        <!-- JSON serialization/deserialization. Version via parent BOM. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>com.fasterxml.jackson.core</groupId>
            <artifactId>jackson-databind</artifactId>
        </dependency>

        <!-- ====================================================================
             TEST DEPENDENCIES (6) — docs/technical-specifications.md L750–L756
             ==================================================================== -->

        <!-- JUnit 5 + Mockito + AssertJ bundle. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-test</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Mockito core is already supplied transitively by spring-boot-starter-test
             (version managed by the Spring Boot BOM). It is ALSO declared explicitly
             here so the maven-dependency-plugin `properties` goal (build section)
             reliably exposes its jar location as the ${org.mockito:mockito-core:jar}
             property, which the Surefire/Failsafe argLine uses to load Mockito as an
             explicit -javaagent. Under Java 25 this prevents Mockito's runtime
             self-attach and the resulting "Java agent loaded dynamically" /
             ByteBuddy dynamic-agent warnings (AAP §0.7.8 zero-warning build). No
             explicit <version> — the BOM keeps it aligned with the bundle above. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.mockito</groupId>
            <artifactId>mockito-core</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Spring Batch job testing utilities. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.batch</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-batch-test</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Spring Security test context utilities. -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.springframework.security</groupId>
            <artifactId>spring-security-test</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>

        <!-- Testcontainers (versions via the imported testcontainers-bom:2.0.3):
             PostgreSQL for JPA integration tests; LocalStack for verifying every
             AWS interaction with zero live dependencies; JUnit 5 lifecycle glue.
             NOTE: Testcontainers 2.x — the version pinned by the blueprint (§0.5.1,
             testcontainers-bom 2.0.3) — renamed every module with a
             "testcontainers-" prefix. The blueprint dependency table (L753–L756)
             listed the legacy 1.x artifact IDs (postgresql / localstack /
             junit-jupiter); those do NOT exist at 2.0.3 (verified 404 on Maven
             Central). The 2.x coordinates below are therefore used so the pinned
             BOM version resolves (verified 200). -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
            <artifactId>testcontainers-postgresql</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
            <artifactId>testcontainers-localstack</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.testcontainers</groupId>
            <artifactId>testcontainers-junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <!-- Stable, version-independent name for the repackaged executable JAR. -->
        <finalName>carddemo-java</finalName>

        <plugins>
            <!-- ================================================================
                 BUILD PLUGINS (5) — docs/technical-specifications.md L762–L766
                 ================================================================ -->

            <!-- Spring Boot repackage: produces the executable (fat) JAR. Plugin
                 version and sensible defaults are inherited from the parent. -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>
                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>
            </plugin>

            <!-- maven-dependency-plugin: the `properties` goal (bound to the
                 `initialize` phase) sets one build property per resolved dependency
                 whose value is that artifact's absolute path in the local repository,
                 e.g. ${org.mockito:mockito-core:jar}. The Surefire/Failsafe argLine
                 below uses that property to load Mockito as an explicit -javaagent so
                 it never self-attaches at runtime under Java 25 (AAP §0.7.8). Version
                 pinned for reproducible, offline builds. -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-dependency-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.8.1</version>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>resolve-dependency-properties</id>
                        <phase>initialize</phase>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>properties</goal>
                        </goals>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>

            <!-- Surefire: UNIT tests only (*Test / *Tests). Integration and E2E
                 classes are excluded here and handled by Failsafe below. The argLine
                 loads Mockito as an explicit Java agent to avoid the Java 25
                 self-attach/ByteBuddy dynamic-agent warnings; `@{argLine}` is the
                 late-evaluated placeholder that preserves the JaCoCo coverage agent
                 injected by `prepare-agent`, and `-Xshare:off` suppresses the
                 "Sharing is only supported..." CDS warning that appending an agent to
                 the bootstrap classpath would otherwise emit. -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>${maven-surefire-failsafe.version}</version>
                <configuration>
                    <argLine>@{argLine} -javaagent:${org.mockito:mockito-core:jar} -Xshare:off</argLine>
                    <includes>
                        <include>**/*Test.java</include>
                        <include>**/*Tests.java</include>
                    </includes>
                    <excludes>
                        <exclude>**/*IT.java</exclude>
                        <exclude>**/integration/**</exclude>
                        <exclude>**/e2e/**</exclude>
                    </excludes>
                </configuration>
            </plugin>

            <!-- Failsafe: INTEGRATION / E2E tests (*IT + integration/ + e2e/),
                 bound to the integration-test/verify phases. Skipped by default
                 (skipITs=true, since these require Docker/Testcontainers); the
                 `integration` profile flips skipITs to false to realize
                 `mvn verify -Pintegration` (tech-spec L979). Its argLine mirrors
                 Surefire's: `@{argLine}` preserves the JaCoCo coverage agent (so
                 integration coverage still appends to the same exec data for a
                 combined figure), plus the explicit Mockito -javaagent and
                 `-Xshare:off` for a warning-free Java 25 run. -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-failsafe-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>${maven-surefire-failsafe.version}</version>
                <configuration>
                    <argLine>@{argLine} -javaagent:${org.mockito:mockito-core:jar} -Xshare:off</argLine>
                    <includes>
                        <include>**/*IT.java</include>
                        <include>**/integration/**/*.java</include>
                        <include>**/e2e/**/*.java</include>
                    </includes>
                    <skipITs>${skipITs}</skipITs>
                </configuration>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>integration-tests</id>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>integration-test</goal>
                            <goal>verify</goal>
                        </goals>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>

            <!-- OWASP dependency-check: fails the build on any CVE with
                 CVSS >= 7.0 (HIGH/CRITICAL), enforcing the "zero critical/high
                 CVE" gate (AAP §0.7.8). The `check` goal binds to the verify
                 phase and scans the full direct + transitive closure. -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.owasp</groupId>
                <artifactId>dependency-check-maven</artifactId>
                <version>${owasp-dependency-check.version}</version>
                <configuration>
                    <failBuildOnCVSS>7</failBuildOnCVSS>
                    <skipProvidedScope>false</skipProvidedScope>
                    <skipRuntimeScope>false</skipRuntimeScope>
                    <!-- OSS Index is an ONLINE-ONLY supplementary analyzer that
                         calls ossindex.sonatype.org and requires Sonatype
                         credentials; in this offline/air-gapped build it returns
                         HTTP 401 and makes the gate non-deterministic. The warmed
                         local NVD cache is the authoritative CVE source and fully
                         covers the "zero critical/high CVE" gate (AAP §0.7.8), so
                         the online OSS Index analyzer is disabled for deterministic
                         offline scanning. (Set autoUpdate=false on the command line
                         to also pin the NVD data to the warmed cache.) -->
                    <ossindexAnalyzerEnabled>false</ossindexAnalyzerEnabled>
                    <!-- Justified suppressions for CPE/scope false positives and
                         not-applicable matches (each scoped to the exact artifact +
                         exact CVE, fully documented). See owasp-suppressions.xml. -->
                    <suppressionFiles>
                        <suppressionFile>${project.basedir}/owasp-suppressions.xml</suppressionFile>
                    </suppressionFiles>
                </configuration>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>owasp-dependency-check</id>
                        <phase>verify</phase>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>check</goal>
                        </goals>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>

            <!-- JaCoCo 0.8.14 (official Java 25 / class-file major 69 support).
                 `prepare-agent` wires the coverage agent into the test JVM via the
                 `argLine` property (consumed by both Surefire and Failsafe); with
                 append=true (the default) unit + integration runs accumulate into a
                 single exec file, yielding COMBINED coverage. The `check` rule
                 enforces >= 80% LINE coverage at the bundle level, satisfying the
                 coverage gate (AAP §0.7.8). report/check are bound to `verify` so
                 they observe both unit and integration coverage. -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.jacoco</groupId>
                <artifactId>jacoco-maven-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>${jacoco.version}</version>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <id>jacoco-prepare-agent</id>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>prepare-agent</goal>
                        </goals>
                    </execution>
                    <execution>
                        <id>jacoco-report</id>
                        <phase>verify</phase>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>report</goal>
                        </goals>
                    </execution>
                    <execution>
                        <id>jacoco-check</id>
                        <phase>verify</phase>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>check</goal>
                        </goals>
                        <configuration>
                            <rules>
                                <rule>
                                    <element>BUNDLE</element>
                                    <limits>
                                        <limit>
                                            <counter>LINE</counter>
                                            <value>COVEREDRATIO</value>
                                            <minimum>0.80</minimum>
                                        </limit>
                                    </limits>
                                </rule>
                            </rules>
                        </configuration>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>

    <profiles>
        <!-- `integration` profile: enables the Failsafe integration/E2E run via
             `mvn verify -Pintegration`. Requires a Docker daemon for Testcontainers
             (PostgreSQL + LocalStack). By default (no profile) only unit tests run. -->
        <profile>
            <id>integration</id>
            <properties>
                <skipITs>false</skipITs>
            </properties>
        </profile>
    </profiles>

</project>
